      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Earlville%2C_Pennsylvania"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town sits along Pennsylvania Route 562 where it meets Manatawny Creek, just west of Boyertown.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Earlville%2C_Pennsylvania"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Because it has no municipal government, Earlville relies on the surrounding townships for local services.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://kids.kiddle.co/Earlville,_Pennsylvania"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Earlville’s territory is divided between Amity Township and Earl Township, both part of Berks County.",
